    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0177" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10564: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-02T14:00:00+03:00">May 2, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>893. I have learned from a member of the French Embassy that when the new French
                        Ambassador<anchor n="26" xml:id="d176-f1"/> called on Molotov he delivered
                    what my informant described as a “speech” dealing with the planned collaboration
                    between France and Germany and indicating his belief in an ultimate German
                    victory and his faith in German promises which I judge was substantially along
                    the line taken by him in his talk with me. My informant stated that upon his
                    return to the Embassy the Ambassador has expressed his surprise and chagrin that
                    Molotov “had <pb facs="0178" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/> not uttered a word during
                    the entire session”, and that short of greeting him on entering the room and
                    saying good-bye he said “nothing”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d176-f1" n="26" xml:id="d176-f1-content">
                <p>Gaston Bergery, successor to Eric Labonne.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
